BT
/F1 8 Tf
11 TL
35 752 Td
( Hardware Support & Troubleshooting) Tj
T*
( What the installer recognizes, changes, and how to investigate failures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( 4. Firmware matching) Tj
T*
( Packages are suggested by detected chipset vendor, not guaranteed exact-card compatibility. The script) Tj
T*
( handles common Intel, Realtek, Broadcom, Atheros/Qualcomm, MediaTek, and Marvell IDs. Depending on the) Tj
T*
( Debian release, it may suggest:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Vendor                                        Common package) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Intel                                         firmware-iwlwifi) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Realtek                                       firmware-realtek) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Broadcom                                      firmware-brcm80211) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Qualcomm / Atheros                            firmware-atheros) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   MediaTek                                      firmware-mediatek or firmware-misc-nonfree) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Marvell                                       firmware-libertas) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( 5. Repository behavior) Tj
T*
( If a required firmware package is unavailable, the installer may add an official Debian non-free-firmware) Tj
T*
( source on systems identified as Debian 12 \(bookworm\) or Debian 13 \(trixie\). The source is written to:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    /etc/apt/sources.list.d/wifi-firmware-autosetup.list) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( Use --no-repo to disable this behavior. The installer does not add third-party driver repositories or install drivers) Tj
T*
( from GitHub.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
( 6. Troubleshooting) Tj
T*
( No Wi-Fi adapter detected: Check BIOS/UEFI settings and whether the adapter is present. Try lspci -nnk) Tj
T*
( \(internal PCI/PCIe\) or lsusb \(USB\), if installed.) Tj
T*
( APT update or installation fails: Confirm Ethernet/tethering, check configured Debian repositories, and) Tj
T*
( ensure system date/time is correct.) Tj
T*
( Firmware installed but Wi-Fi is missing: Reboot, then check the adapter and whether it is blocked:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    ip link) Tj
T*
(    rfkill list wifi) Tj
T*
(    sudo dmesg | grep -iE "firmware|wifi|wlan" | tail -n 30) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(    Limitations: Some Broadcom and Realtek adapters need separate kernel drivers, newer kernels, or a different) Tj
T*
(    firmware package. USB adapters with generic descriptions may not be auto-detected. The script does not guarantee) Tj
T*
(    support for every card or automatically join a wireless network.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Wi-Fi Firmware | Debian / Raspberry Pi Desktop on Dell PC                                                              2/2) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
